  {
   "assumption": "Management is 'average' and capital allocation is only 'mixed'",
   "why_questionable": "$12.1B was spent on buybacks at an average of $97.57 and the stock is now at $34.61, a roughly 65% loss on roughly the whole current market cap's worth of buyback. Options (76.8M at $96.44 strike) are deep out of the money, which weakens equity-based retention. The CEO's own stake is minimal and pay is about $36M while earnings fall. The dividend is uncovered, and a new CFO means the capital return policy is uncertain."
