Filings: {"business_summary":"NIKE, Inc. designs, develops, markets and sells athletic footwear, apparel, equipment and accessories under the NIKE, Jordan and Converse brands. Sales go through wholesale accounts and NIKE Direct (owned stores plus digital). It describes itself as the world's largest seller of athletic footwear and apparel (SEC 10-K 2026-07-15, Item 1). FY2026 (year ended May 31, 2026) revenue was $46.4B, flat reported and down 2% currency-neutral. Net income was $3.1B and diluted EPS $2.10 (SEC 10-K). The company is in a multi-year reset: it is rebalancing footwear supply, repositioning NIKE Digital as full-price, reinvesting in wholesale and cutting costs. Greater China and Converse are weak (Greater China -26% and Converse -28% currency-neutral in Q1 FY27, SEC 10-Q 2026-10-02). In October 2026 NIKE announced the 'Pace' program: about $1.0B of further pre-tax charges and about $2.5B of cumulative savings through FY2031 (SEC 10-Q). Stock price is $34.61 and market cap about $51.4B (Market Data).","key_figures":[{"metric":"Revenue","value":"$46,398M (FY25 $46,309M; FY24 $51,362M)","period":"FY2026 (May 31, 2026)","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-07-15), Consolidated Statements of Income"},{"metric":"Gross margin","value":"42.9% (FY25 42.7%; FY24 44.6%)","period":"FY2026","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-07-15), MD&A"},{"metric":"Operating income (gross profit less selling & admin expense)","value":"$3,797M (FY25 $3,702M; FY24 $6,311M)","period":"FY2026","source":"Market Data history; reconciles to SEC 10-K ($19,911M gross profit less $16,114M S&A)"},{"metric":"Net income / diluted EPS","value":"$3,108M / $2.10 (FY25 $3,219M / $2.16)","period":"FY2026","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-07-15)"},{"metric":"EBIT and EBIT margin","value":"$3,850M; 8.3% (FY24 12.7%)","period":"FY2026","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-07-15), Non-GAAP table"},{"metric":"Operating cash flow","value":"$2,868M (FY25 $3,698M; FY24 $7,429M)","period":"FY2026","source":"SEC 10-K (2026-07-15), Cash Flow Statement